WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:25.240
On the 11th of April of 2015 a historical
meeting took place between Raul Castro, the

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.220
president of Cuba, and Barack Obama.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.510
It was celebrated in Panama and it was the
first bilateral meeting of the US and Cuba

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.350
President's in 50 years.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.930
Four months earlier, both leaders had announced
they would remake relations between the two

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:46.860
governments.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.040
And as they said they would do, so it was
done.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.010
In just a short period of time, the first
changes were made, and relations between both

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.030
countries started to return to normal.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:01:00.080
Now, it does seem like we say this a lot on
this channel, but the arrival of Donald Trump

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.210
to the White House, well, it changed everything... again.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.560
The new president of the United States has
ordered that the US steps back from most of

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.260
the changes that Obama had initiated with
Cuba.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.700
So, the question might be: Why is he doing
this?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.950
What does he expect?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.729
And what are the consequences of this new
policy?

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:22.469
We're going to look at all of these questions in this video, but before we do, let's have

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:27.580
a look at this history of relations between
these two countries...

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.009
(THE EMBARGO)
After the so-called 'Cuban Revolution'

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:38.649
had taken place against Batista's dictatorship, the new government in the island led by Fidel

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:45.439
Castro soon started to nationalize every kind
of capital good and company: land, hotels,

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:48.399
factories... everything was up for grab by
the government.

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:53.770
So the Cuban Revolution ended on the 1st of
January 1959, and already by May, the government

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.409
had begun huge expropriations all across the
country.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:03.360
Now, as you can probably imagine, this is
something that the US did not take very well.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.940
There were thousands of lawsuits filed in
the U.S., which had close relations with Cuba

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.020
at the time.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:13.750
Further, if this wasn't enough to upset
the U.S., the Soviet Union was already getting

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.610
on well with Fidel Castro.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:22.250
(It was in this situation when, as a penalty,
Washington passed the first trade embargo

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:28.200
against the island, an embargo that slowly
grew stronger as the relations of these countries

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.269
got worse).

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:35.820
In fact, after the missile crisis of 1962,
Kennedy even limited US travel to Cuba.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.540
Since then, and with the exception of a short
period of better relations under the governments

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.900
of Ford and Carter, the various governments
of the United States have kept the embargo

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:49.650
and the policy of isolating Cuba economically
in place.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:54.360
Ronald Reagan labelled the island as a sponsor
of terrorism and later Bill Clinton made restrictions

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.120
even more severe and the embargo became law.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.790
Since then, travelling to Cuba, investing
in Cuba, or doing business with the Cuban

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:06.099
government has been very limited for Americans.

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:12.049
Well, that is, until Barack Obama came to
office.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:17.860
(On February 2008, Fidel passed the power
to his brother Raul Castro.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:22.430
The same year the elections took place and
Obama said it was time to use a different

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.980
approach with Cuba, it was time to repair
diplomatic relations between both countries).

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:33.170
Obama didn't want to wait and, shortly after
he arrived in the White House, he softened

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.590
some of the restrictions in place on Cuba...

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:40.069
For example, he allowed Cubans in the US to
send money to the island and he started to

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:42.500
allow US citizens to travel to Cuba.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.890
Many more things followed these first gestures.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.680
During the years Obama was in office, many
restrictions against Cuba were reduced.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.569
In 2014, both countries announced the reestablishment
of diplomatic relations and, in December of

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:56.989
that same year, Raul Castro and Obama met
in Panama.

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:10.459
Significant progress was being made.

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:22.210
And that is how two great moments took place, in 2015

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:27.780
the embassies reopened in both countries and, in March of 2016, Air Force One landed in

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:40.920
Havana for the first time in history - 
Cuba hadn't hosted a sitting American president

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.020
since 1928.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:49.100
'A policy of isolation designed for the
Cold War made little sense in the 21st Century.'

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.890
The embargo was only hurting the Cuban people, instead of helping them.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.760
It's time to lift the embargo.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.400
It is time now for us to leave the past behind.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.991
It is time for us to look forward to the future together'.

00:05:00.991 --> 00:05:03.460
Obama's Speech to the Cuban People

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:09.240
Obama's new policies towards Cuba were taking over... and even though the embargo laws were

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.170
technically still in force, the Obama administration managed to find legal loopholes to allow the

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:18.010
relations between these two countries to be something close to normal.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:21.580
When Obama left the White House, Americans could travel freely to Cuba, immigrants could

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:26.210
sent unlimited money back to the country,
American companies could invest in Cuba, and

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.470
even planes of American companies frequently
landed in Jose Marti International

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.240
Airport... The new relationship was working.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:39.160
But, then Donald Trump became president of the United States, and as we already mentioned�

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.220
everything changed.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:53.310
(TRUMP AND CUBA)
On the 16th June 2017, Trump decided to take

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:58.000
this new policy back... and he did so in a
neighbourhood of Miami called Little Havana:

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.470
(Effective immediately, I am canceling
the last administration.s completely one-sided

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.690
deal with Cuba), 16th June
2017.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:08.900
As soon as he finished his speech, Trump signed
guidelines for his so called 'new policy'

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.900
with Cuba...

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.970
But, after a 50 year embargo with the country
it could hardly be described as 'new'...

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:21.300
(Trump won't completely reverse it, many
of Obama's policies will be maintained,

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:26.200
like the opening of embassies and the commercial
flights between the two countries).

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.100
However, from now on, trips of Americans to
Cuba will be limited, they won't be able

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:36.420
to go individually, and any relationship with
GAESA, a holding group directed by the government

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.850
(which controls more than 50% of Cuban economy),
will be forbidden.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:44.960
But don't think that Trump has always had
a hard-line attitude towards Cuba... quite

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.960
the opposite in fact!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:50.940
In 1998, he tried to build a hotel in the
island contradicting the embargo and at the

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:56.070
beginning of 2016 he supported Obama new policies
towards the country...

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:00.560
But we think that Trump's attitude towards
Cuba could be a mistake... so let's have

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:07.940
a look at why...
(TRUMP'S MISTAKE)

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:15.320
Let's make one thing really clear: the embargo
against Cuba has been a total failure...

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:21.860
(The U.S. embargo, blocking all trade and
investment with Cuba for the past 55 years,

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:22.860
has not worked.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.140
It has failed to isolate the Cuban government,
failed to regain any nationalized property

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:31.800
and succeeded in giving an excuse to the Castro
government for its abuses and economic mismanagement.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.440
PAUL D. EATON y DAVID L. MCGINNIS)
For more than 50 years, the embargo has been

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.220
completely useless, it hasn't accomplished
anything and, on top of that, the Cuban government

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:44.460
has used it as an excuse to justify their
poor economic situation...

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.410
But, wait just a second, because this is not
the end of it, not even close.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.840
Reversing Obama's policies is a mistake
for several reasons:

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:58.000
Importantly: Improved relations with the US
have meant better security for the United

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.000
States!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.720
Obama signed several co-operation agreements
and, since 2015, Cuban authorities have given

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.200
information on drug and human trafficking
to the U.S..

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:12.420
But, on the other hand, Russia and China have
set their eyes on the island again:

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:18.270
(Russia says it may reopen Soviet-era military
bases in Cuba - The Telegraph).

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.581
You can probably imagine what a blow this
would be for the national security of the

00:08:21.581 --> 00:08:23.890
United States...

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:28.620
This is why making relations more difficult
means nothing more than forcing the Cuban

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:32.630
government to seek better relations with Moscow
or Beijing.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.669
Not exactly a brilliant option for the US.

00:08:35.669 --> 00:08:41.060
And, oh, there is so much more... Trump's
new policy will only damage the interests

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.750
of many American companies, as well as put
at risk the major changes that are taking

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:51.680
place on the island''...
(HOW IS CUBA CHANGING?)

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.390
Since Raul Castro came to power, he has admitted
that Cuba needs a change of direction, and

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.780
that the Cuban model simply is not working.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:04.230
As some people say, he wants to emulate China:
be open to the world but maintain control.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:09.750
The truth is that, up until now, changes have
been scarce and slow'... but even so these

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:14.339
changes could be felt, and now that Venezuela
can no longer help the island, these changes

00:09:14.339 --> 00:09:16.819
have become more and more urgent.

00:09:16.819 --> 00:09:22.120
Let's have a look at what has happened since
2011 when reforms took place and freelance

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.220
entrepreneurship was made a lot easier:

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:31.079
(Since 2011, the number of self-employed workers
in Cuba is four times bigger and today the

00:09:31.079 --> 00:09:34.810
number exceeds half a million workers; the
government has also allowed private farming

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:39.210
for small farmers; and restaurants and small
tourism businesses are growing and spreading

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.930
across the country).

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:45.810
And Obama's openness has certainly helped
this process.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:50.199
For example, almost all private businesses
in Cuba are working off money coming in from

00:09:50.199 --> 00:09:55.550
abroad: AirBnb already has 22,000 apartments,
houses, or rooms, available in Cuba.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:00.829
Further, we shouldn't forget about less tangible
things like the exchange of ideas, mutual

00:10:00.829 --> 00:10:04.399
knowledge, and the strengthening of the private
sector.

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:10.249
'Every dollar left in the hands of cab drivers,
hotel workers, waitresses, and valets is a

00:10:10.249 --> 00:10:15.449
show of what awaits Cubans if they reject
socialism.'- Rand Paul

00:10:15.449 --> 00:10:20.350
Take a look at China, and compare the country
as it is today to the country it was during

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.390
Mao's time.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.949
Since the country opened itself up to the
world, hundreds of million of people have

00:10:24.949 --> 00:10:26.560
left poverty behind.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.009
Yes, China, like Cuba, is still a terrible
dictatorship, but thanks to their open policy,

00:10:32.009 --> 00:10:36.620
the Chinese have today more freedom and a
better standard of living than they have ever

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.620
had before...

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:47.500
The short of it is that the embargo policy
has failed, and Trump's insistence in going

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.399
back to it is not going to achieve anything
but the weakening of the security of the United

00:10:52.399 --> 00:10:56.499
States, lead to further poverty in Cuba, and
prevent the changes that are happening on

00:10:56.499 --> 00:10:57.499
the island.

00:10:57.499 --> 00:11:02.829
In February 2018, Castro is going to leave
power and this is not the moment for the US

00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:05.209
to take a step back.

00:11:05.209 --> 00:11:11.050
In order to justify his decision, Trump says
he wants to defend Human Rights, which is

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:15.970
nice but, don't you think it is a bit hypocritical
to defend Cuba's embargo while, at the same

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.250
time, he hugs the leaders of Saudi Arabia?

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:21.870
Are Human rights not important there?

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:27.870
Importantly: 10 Republican politicians have
already criticized this course-change with

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:28.870
Cuba.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:34.499
'Any policy change that diminishes the ability
of Americans to travel freely to Cuba is not

00:11:34.499 --> 00:11:38.220
in the best interests of the United States
or the Cuban people."

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:42.829
- U.S. Senator Jeff Flake (R-AZ)
But now we'd love to know what you think!

00:11:42.829 --> 00:11:46.819
Please leaves your comments below and also
feel free to answer the survey: Should Donald

00:11:46.819 --> 00:11:49.959
Trump reverse Obama's policies towards Cuba?

